        "original_id": "f47b8da5-1426-573b-8bbe-bcf9ecce3c0f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Markus Feehily, Bobby Fuller, Randy Fuller\n- Organizations: The Bobby Fuller Four, Westlife\n- Products: Fire\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, guitarist, bass player, vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Bobby Fuller was born on October 22, 1942, and died on July 18, 1966.\n- Bobby Fuller was an American rock singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Bobby Fuller was best known for \"Love's Made a Fool of You\" and for his cover of \"I Fought the Law\" recorded with The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Randy Fuller was born on January 29, 1944.\n- Randy Fuller is an American rock singer, songwriter, and bass player.\n- Randy Fuller is best known for performing with his older brother Bobby Fuller in the 1960s rock group The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Markus Feehily was born on 28 May 1980.\n- Markus Feehily, formerly known as Mark Feehily, is an Irish singer and songwriter.\n- Fire is the debut solo studio album by Markus Feehily.\n- Markus Feehily is a former vocalist of Westlife.",
